#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:3
msgid "Web Page Caching"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:5
msgid ""
"CodeIgniter lets you cache your pages in order to achieve maximum "
"performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:8
msgid ""
"Although CodeIgniter is quite fast, the amount of dynamic information you"
" display in your pages will correlate directly to the server resources, "
"memory, and processing cycles utilized, which affect your page load "
"speeds. By caching your pages, since they are saved in their fully "
"rendered state, you can achieve performance much closer to that of static"
" web pages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:20
msgid "How Does Caching Work?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:22
msgid ""
"Caching can be enabled on a per-page basis, and you can set the length of"
" time that a page should remain cached before being refreshed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:25
msgid ""
"Per-page means per URI. Since v4.5.0, the HTTP method of the request is "
"also taken into account. This means that the same URI will be cached "
"separately if the HTTP method is different."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:29
msgid ""
"When a page is loaded for the first time, the page will be cached using "
"the currently configured cache engine. On subsequent page loads, the "
"cache will be retrieved and sent to the requesting user's browser."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:33
msgid ""
"If it has expired, it will be deleted and refreshed before being sent to "
"the browser."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:36
msgid ""
"The Benchmark tag is not cached so you can still view your page load "
"speed when caching is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:40
msgid "Configuring Caching"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:43
msgid "Setting Cache Engine"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:45
msgid ""
"Before using Web Page Caching, you must set the cache engine up by "
"editing **app/Config/Cache.php**. See :ref:`libraries-caching-"
"configuring-the-cache` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:50
msgid "Setting $cacheQueryString"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:52
msgid ""
"You can set whether or not to include the query string when generating "
"the cache with ``Config\\Cache::$cacheQueryString``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:55 ../../source/general/caching.rst:76
msgid "Valid options are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:57
msgid ""
"``false``: (default) Disabled. The query string is not taken into "
"account; the same cache is returned for requests with the same URI path "
"but different query strings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:60
msgid ""
"``true``: Enabled, take all query parameters into account. Be aware that "
"this may result in numerous cache generated for the same page over and "
"over again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:63
msgid ""
"**array**: Enabled, but only take into account the specified list of "
"query parameters. E.g., ``['q', 'page']``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:69
msgid "Setting $cacheStatusCodes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:73
msgid ""
"You can control which HTTP response status codes are allowed to be cached"
" with ``Config\\Cache::$cacheStatusCodes``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:78
msgid ""
"``[]``: (default) Cache all HTTP status codes. This maintains backward "
"compatibility but may cache temporary error pages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:80
msgid ""
"``[200]``: (Recommended) Only cache successful responses. This prevents "
"caching of error pages (404, 500, etc.) that should be temporary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:82
msgid "array of status codes: Cache only specific status codes. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:84
msgid "``[200, 404]``: Cache successful responses and not found pages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:85
msgid "``[200, 404, 410]``: Cache successful responses and specific error codes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:86
msgid "``[200, 201, 202, 203, 204]``: All 2xx successful responses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:88
msgid ""
"Using an empty array ``[]`` may cache temporary error pages (404, 500, "
"etc). For production applications, consider restricting this to ``[200]``"
" to avoid caching errors that should be temporary. For example, a cached "
"404 page would remain cached even after the resource is created, until "
"the cache expires."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:93
msgid ""
"Regardless of this setting, ``DownloadResponse`` and ``RedirectResponse``"
" instances are never cached by the ``PageCache`` filter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:97
msgid "Enabling Caching"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:99
msgid ""
"To enable caching, put the following tag in any of your controller "
"methods:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:104
msgid ""
"Where ``$n`` is the number of **seconds** you wish the page to remain "
"cached between refreshes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:107
msgid ""
"The above tag can go anywhere within a method. It is not affected by the "
"order that it appears, so place it wherever it seems most logical to you."
" Once the tag is in place, your pages will begin being cached."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:111
msgid ""
"If you change configuration options that might affect your output, you "
"have to manually delete your cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:115
msgid "Deleting Caches"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:117
msgid ""
"If you no longer wish to cache a page you can remove the caching tag and "
"it will no longer be refreshed when it expires."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/general/caching.rst:120
msgid ""
"Removing the tag will not delete the cache immediately. It will have to "
"expire normally."
msgstr ""

